{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Hanging out With Friends", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Reminiscing About the Good Old Days", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Used to and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have rather similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, there is an important difference between  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while  <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following examples: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "However, when <span class=\"strong\">would</span> replaces <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, the same example becomes ungrammatical:<br><br>  <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India.</span> (not correct)<br> <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I used to write down every single step of my favorite recipes!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We would try them out with my friends at school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did you use to write down the recipes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wouldn't show them to anyone!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Be careful of the question form of <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">Did you <span class=\"strong\">use to</span> go to India every summer?</span> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<ol><li>We use the Present Perfect tense for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.</li><li>We use the Simple Past tense for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Have you always kept a cooking diary?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The time period goes up to the present.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I was a picky eater as a kid. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I am not a picky eater anymore.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "engaging", "type": "name"}, {"content": " captivating and appealing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to write an engaging piece about friendships.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about childhood memories.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "interviewee ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is interviewed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're my next interviewee for the article I'm writing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to write information in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you ever kept a cooking diary?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "step", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one part in a series of actions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I used to write down every single step of my favorite recipes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "otherwise", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in another situation; apart from that", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(conjunction)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm glad you like cooking. We wouldn't be friends otherwise!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "picky", "type": "name"}, {"content": " difficult; fastidious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was a picky eater as a kid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a diary entry (10-14 lines) about how your life was in high school.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write about what you used to do regularly.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your entry aloud to a partner. Talk about your partner's entry.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "con